   "availability": "in_stock",
   "description": "B/1 DAZZLE Standard Dial The B/1 Dazzle, a new expression of the brand’s architectural design language, inspired by the radical visual language of First World War dazzle camouflage. Dazzle was never intended to conceal. Applied to ships in fractured fields of contrasting geometry, it was designed to confuse the eye, to disrupt proportion, direction and speed. The B/1 Dazzle translates that idea to the wrist. Its Grade 5 titanium case and integrated bracelet are covered in an irregular composition of intersecting lines and planes. Alternating frosted and satin-brushed finishes catch the light differently, causing the pattern to shift as the wrist moves. Form appears to break apart and reassemble; edges become uncertain and the watch’s familiar silhouette begins to disappear. It is built into the surfaces of the watch, moving continuously across the case and bracelet and transforming the entire object into a single sculptural composition. No two viewpoints are quite the same. At the centre is Toledano & Chan’s signature asymmetrical sapphire crystal. Cut as a dramatic architectural volume rather than a conventional transparent cover, it refracts and distorts the dial beneath it. The dial itself continues the dazzle composition extending the visual disruption through every layer of the watch. The Toledano & Chan B/1 Dazzle will be produced in a limited edition of 200 pieces. 188 standard dials: $7700 Movement: Sellita SW100 Case and bracelet: Grade 5 titanium To achieve the Dazzle pattern, the case and bracelet are first CNC engraved, then the pattern is frosted with diamond dust, and finally, brushing applied. Swiss made Release date: October 24th Embargo ends: October 12th Watches will be available at toledanoandchan.com, Antoine de Macedo (Paris), Collective Horology (California), The Turkish Watch Guy (Istanbul), Berdanini (Milan) and Exquisite Timepieces (Florida)",
